      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you're feeling the weight of that quiet, and it's a heavy thing to carry when it turns into a cage. Don't mistake safety for peace; sometimes the quiet just amplifies how trapped you feel. If the walls are closing in, maybe the only way to stop them is to make a very small, deliberate change to the structure itself. Just one small act of letting the outside in, or letting yourself out, might be the only thing that feels like a real option right now.",
